  "id": "social-instinct",
  "term": "social instinct",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, social instinct means an inborn tendency toward social conduct that was regarded as a source of virtue. It refers to behavior that can appear moral before a person has reflective understanding or deliberate choice about good and evil.",
